BUNDLED IN THE APK (personal builds)
------------------------------------

  app/src/main/assets/patches/   natdex-emerald.bps, natdex-firered.bps
  app/src/main/assets/types/     19 type icons, from besteon/Ironmon-Tracker
                                 (images/types), drawn 30x12 by its
                                 Drawing.drawTypeIcon
  app/src/main/assets/status/    6 status icons, same source
  app/src/main/assets/gen4sprites/  986 Pokemon sprites (493 + shiny), from
                                 Brian0255/NDS-Ironmon-Tracker
                                 (images/pokemonIconSets/hgsssprites).
                                 Needed because Gen 4 art lives in compressed
                                 archives inside the ROM.
  app/src/main/assets/gbasprites/  1285 Pokemon sprites, 32x32, indexed by
                                 the ROM's own species id (Gen 3 internal
                                 ordering continued past 411), NOT by national
                                 dex number. 1-411 from
                                 besteon/Ironmon-Tracker (images/pokemonUpdated);
                                 412-1285 from CyanSMP64/NatDexExtension
                                 (natdex/sprites_mons), covered by the written
                                 permission quoted at the top of this file.
                                 Used on the Nat. Dex builds. Vanilla
                                 FireRed/Emerald still decode art from the ROM,
                                 so the card shows the art of the ROM actually
                                 being played.
                                 Bundled because the Nat. Dex ROMs publish no
                                 front-pic table address, so there is nothing to
                                 decode and every card rendered blank.
  app/src/main/assets/presets/   FRLG Kaizo, RSE Kaizo, RSE NatDex v1.2 Kaizo,
                                 FRLG NatDex v1.2 Kaizo, DPPt Kaizo (Gen 4)

  These ship inside the APK so a fresh install can patch and randomize with no
  file hunting. The patches are extracted on demand, the presets on first run,
  and an imported copy always wins so a newer release can be dropped in without
  an app update.

  ** The sprites and icons above are Pokemon artwork; the tracker projects are
  GPL-3.0 but the art is Nintendo's. Same standing as the patches: fine for a
  local personal build, and a public release must remove them or obtain rights.

  ** Licence status: Cyan's grant above is recorded as covering the extension's
  Pokemon/move data and sprites, and explicitly NOT "anything else". The .bps
  patches and the Nat. Dex .rnqs are his files and fall outside that recorded
  scope. This is a LOCAL, personal, undistributed build, so bundling them is
  not redistribution. Before ANY public release, either get that grant extended
  in writing (record it above, the way the first one is recorded) or remove
  these assets and go back to one-time import. Condition 3 still holds
  regardless: no ROM is bundled, only patches. **

  The two vanilla GBA Kaizo presets are the official IronMON settings published
  in UTDZac's public gist for players to use.

  "DPPt Kaizo.rnqs" is DiamondPearlPlatinum_Kaizo.rnqs, copied unmodified from
  Brian0255/NDS-Ironmon-Tracker (ironmon_tracker/settings/). That project is
  GPL-3.0 and the file is a randomizer settings string published for players to
  use, not game content. It is bundled for the same reason as the others: so a
  fresh install can start a Gen 4 run without hunting for a file.


